---
// DIAGRAM for 7.2: the metrics of one experiment. One primary metric decides; secondary metrics explain;
// guardrails must not get worse.
---
<figure class="cs-fig mlf">
  <span class="cs-figtag">Metrics for a checkout test</span>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 640 250" role="img" aria-label="A tree with the goal at the top, the primary metric below it, then secondary metrics and guardrail metrics">
    <rect class="box" x="220" y="8" width="200" height="44" rx="10" /><text x="320" y="35" text-anchor="middle" class="b">Goal: more completed orders</text>
    <rect class="acc" x="200" y="80" width="240" height="50" rx="10" /><text x="320" y="102" text-anchor="middle" class="b">Primary: purchase conversion</text><text x="320" y="120" text-anchor="middle" class="mu">decides ship / don't ship</text>
    <rect class="box" x="10" y="165" width="300" height="78" rx="10" /><text x="160" y="186" text-anchor="middle" class="b">Secondary (explain why)</text><text x="160" y="206" text-anchor="middle" class="mu">checkout starts · payment errors</text><text x="160" y="224" text-anchor="middle" class="mu">average order value · time to pay</text>
    <rect class="box" x="330" y="165" width="300" height="78" rx="10" /><text x="480" y="186" text-anchor="middle" class="b">Guardrails (must not worsen)</text><text x="480" y="206" text-anchor="middle" class="mu">refunds · support contacts</text><text x="480" y="224" text-anchor="middle" class="mu">page load time · revenue per visitor</text>
    <path class="ln" d="M320 52 V80" /><path class="ln" d="M300 130 L160 165" /><path class="ln" d="M340 130 L480 165" />
    <text x="632" y="247" text-anchor="end" class="wm">fibub.com</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>Write this tree before the test starts. Only the primary metric decides the outcome; secondary metrics help explain it; a guardrail that gets clearly worse can stop a launch even if the primary metric wins.</figcaption>
</figure>
